{
  "an4.73:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.73 ",
  "an4.73:0.2": "8.  Sure Bet ",
  "an4.73:0.3": "A True Person ",
  "an4.73:1.1": "“Mendicants, an untrue person can be known by four qualities. ",
  "an4.73:1.2": "What four? ",
  "an4.73:1.3": "To start with, an untrue person speaks ill of another even when not asked, let alone when asked. ",
  "an4.73:1.4": "But when summoned for questioning they speak ill of another in full detail, not leaving anything out. ",
  "an4.73:1.5": "That’s how to know that this is an untrue person. ",
  "an4.73:2.1": "Furthermore, an untrue person doesn’t speak well of another even when asked, let alone when not asked. ",
  "an4.73:2.2": "But when summoned for questioning they speak well of another without giving the full details, leaving many things out. ",
  "an4.73:2.3": "That’s how to know that this is an untrue person. ",
  "an4.73:3.1": "Furthermore, an untrue person doesn’t speak ill of themselves even when asked, let alone when not asked. ",
  "an4.73:3.2": "But when summoned for questioning they speak ill of themselves without giving the full details, leaving many things out. ",
  "an4.73:3.3": "That’s how to know that this is an untrue person. ",
  "an4.73:4.1": "Furthermore, an untrue person speaks well of themselves even when not asked, let alone when asked. ",
  "an4.73:4.2": "But when summoned for questioning they speak well of themselves in full detail, not leaving anything out. ",
  "an4.73:4.3": "That’s how to know that this is an untrue person. ",
  "